[gd_scene load_steps=19 format=3 uid="uid://wardbfixdisp001"]

; Wall-mounted medication dispenser. Canonical size 0.55W x 0.75H x 0.16D,
; origin at the centre of the volume, faceplate faces -Z. Composite so it
; reads as a fixture rather than a flat wall panel (see godot/MIGRATION_NOTES.md
; and src/game/world.ts:637 for why a plain box fails against the plaster
; shaders): dark body, a cream faceplate with a cross + MEDICATION text, a
; recessed amber-glow dispensing slot, and a tray lip below it. Warm amber is
; the dispenser's accent colour, distinct from the keypad's cool cyan, so the
; two never read as the same fixture from across a dim room.
;
; Realism pass (see godot/fixtures/_gen/gen_bevel_meshes.gd): body, faceplate
; and tray are baked chamfered-box meshes (real bevelled edges, not plain
; BoxMesh corners) instead of the flat slabs this started as. The faceplate
; reads as a two-leaf glazed cabinet door: a dark seam strip splits it, two
; vertical hinge barrels sit on the left edge, a latch box sits right of
; centre, and four corner screws stud the frame — all fixtures/hardware_mat
; (dark worn metal, metallic pinned low per MIGRATION_NOTES). Two blank
; notice-card plates flank the dispensing slot per the reference photos.
; The faceplate is offset +1cm off dead-centre and the right notice card is
; tilted a few degrees — small manufactured-object asymmetry per the brief,
; kept well inside the body so it reads as "installed", not "broken".
;
; Visuals only — no collision, no gameplay script. The room generator supplies
; the Area3D + CollisionShape3D this gets instanced under.

